# Stripe: official SDK, blocking adapter, virtual-thread offload

Talk to Stripe with the official **stripe-java** SDK (`StripeClient`), not a Quarkus REST client. Wrap `StripeClient` in an adapter. The adapter is **blocking**. That is the cost of the SDK; do not pretend the HTTP call is non-blocking.

## Thin adapter — no business logic

The SDK wrapper **must never, under any circumstances**, contain business logic. It **must** be **very thin**: call the SDK, populate a repo type from the result, return.

The adapter **may** populate a model with data returned from the SDK (copy fields). Copying inbound DTO fields onto SDK request params is the same: field copy, not a transformation. It **must not** aggregate, summarise, or otherwise transform that data. Those transformations belong in a **business layer**, not the adapter.

The adapter **must not** return SDK models (`PaymentIntent`, `Customer`, or any other `com.stripe` type). It **must** return a DTO class **defined in this repo**. Do not leak SDK types on the adapter method signature (parameters or return type).

Because the wrapper is that thin, **mock it** in automated tests. Use **`@QuarkusTest`** and Mockito **`@InjectMock`** on the adapter. Inject the real caller with CDI (`@Inject`). Return repo DTOs. Do not use `MockitoExtension`, `@Mock`, or `@InjectMocks`. Do not mock `StripeClient`. Do not call Stripe. Do not stub `com.stripe` models. Fixture values are **UUIDs** so tests stay isolated under parallel runs. `@QuarkusTest` still boots the app. Put **every** property override in `getConfigOverrides()` — not only `STRIPE_API_KEY`. **Use this instead of a test `application.yaml`** (or `application.yml` / `application.properties`). Do not add those files for test overrides. Do **not** copy shared keys onto every test class. Put shared overrides (including `STRIPE_API_KEY`, so `${STRIPE_API_KEY:${sm//…}}` does not call Secret Manager) on a **reusable** `QuarkusTestProfile`. Point tests at that profile with `@TestProfile`. Test-only extras: a subclass that merges `super.getConfigOverrides()` with more keys.

## API key

Evaluate the Stripe secret key in this order. Do not hardcode it. Do not load it in `@PostConstruct`. Add `quarkus-config-yaml` and `quarkus-google-cloud-secret-manager`. Do not also define the same key in `application.properties`.

1. **Environment variable** `STRIPE_API_KEY` — overrides everything else. Use this for local runs.
2. **`application.yaml`** — `${STRIPE_API_KEY:${sm//stripe-api-key}}`. Same env var; GCP Secret Manager only if that variable is **unset**.

An **empty** env var counts as set (it does not fall through to Secret Manager). If the env var is unset and Secret Manager cannot be read, **startup must fail**. Do not catch that. `${sm//stripe-api-key}` is the secret id (latest, default project). Inject `stripe.api-key` into the `StripeClient` producer.

## Thread policy

The adapter does **not** choose a thread. No `@RunOnVirtualThread`, no `@Blocking`, on the adapter.

`@RunOnVirtualThread` is **optional** and belongs on the **caller** (the JAX-RS resource method, or other entrypoint) **only when that caller would otherwise run on the event loop**. If the caller is already on a virtual thread, or is not on the event loop, call the adapter with no extra annotation.

Event-loop paths must **scale**. Do **not** offload Stripe with `@Blocking` or any other hop onto the capped OS worker pool. A blocking signature without `@RunOnVirtualThread` is the worker pool — that is not acceptable for Stripe.

A resource that needs the SDK result **cannot** stay a `Uni` event-loop method. Give it a concrete return type and `@RunOnVirtualThread`. Do not wrap the SDK in `Uni` on the event loop. Do not mix `@RunOnVirtualThread` with a `Uni` (or `CompletionStage` / `Multi`) return type.

Default `HttpURLConnection` can pin a carrier. Do not "fix" pinning with `@Blocking`.

## Example

```yaml
stripe:
  api-key: ${STRIPE_API_KEY:${sm//stripe-api-key}}
```

```kotlin
data class CreatePaymentIntentCommand(val amount: Long, val currency: String)

data class PaymentIntentDto(val id: String, val status: String)

@ApplicationScoped
class StripeClientProducer {
    @Produces
    @ApplicationScoped
    fun stripeClient(
        @ConfigProperty(name = "stripe.api-key") apiKey: String,
    ): StripeClient = StripeClient(apiKey)
}

@ApplicationScoped
class StripePaymentAdapter(
    private val stripeClient: StripeClient,
) {
    fun createPaymentIntent(command: CreatePaymentIntentCommand): PaymentIntentDto {
        val created = stripeClient.v1().paymentIntents().create(toStripeParams(command))
        return PaymentIntentDto(id = created.id, status = created.status)
    }
}

@Path("/payments")
class PaymentResource(
    private val stripePaymentAdapter: StripePaymentAdapter,
) {
    @POST
    @RunOnVirtualThread
    fun create(request: CreatePaymentRequest): PaymentIntentDto =
        stripePaymentAdapter.createPaymentIntent(
            CreatePaymentIntentCommand(amount = request.amount, currency = request.currency),
        )
}
```

```kotlin
open class StripeTestProfile : QuarkusTestProfile {
    override fun getConfigOverrides(): Map<String, String> =
        mapOf("STRIPE_API_KEY" to UUID.randomUUID().toString())
}

@QuarkusTest
@TestProfile(StripeTestProfile::class)
class ChargeServiceTest {

    @InjectMock
    lateinit var stripePaymentAdapter: StripePaymentAdapter

    @Inject
    lateinit var chargeService: ChargeService

    @Test
    fun usesAdapterDto() {
        val paymentIntentId = UUID.randomUUID().toString()
        whenever(stripePaymentAdapter.createPaymentIntent(any()))
            .thenReturn(PaymentIntentDto(id = paymentIntentId, status = "requires_payment_method"))

        val result = chargeService.charge(CreatePaymentIntentCommand(amount = 1200, currency = "gbp"))

        assertEquals(paymentIntentId, result.id)
    }
}
```

## Do not

```kotlin
@ApplicationScoped
class StripePaymentAdapter(
    private val stripeClient: StripeClient,
) {
    @RunOnVirtualThread
    fun createPaymentIntent(params: PaymentIntentCreateParams): PaymentIntent =
        stripeClient.v1().paymentIntents().create(params)

    fun totalsForCustomer(customerId: String): Long {
        val list = stripeClient.v1().paymentIntents().list(
            PaymentIntentListParams.builder().setCustomer(customerId).build(),
        )
        return list.data.sumOf { it.amount }
    }
}

@Path("/payments")
class PaymentResource(
    private val stripePaymentAdapter: StripePaymentAdapter,
) {
    @POST
    @Blocking
    fun create(request: CreatePaymentRequest): PaymentResponse =
        PaymentResponse(stripePaymentAdapter.createPaymentIntent(toParams(request)).id)

    @POST
    @Path("reactive")
    fun createReactive(request: CreatePaymentRequest): Uni<PaymentResponse> =
        Uni.createFrom().item {
            PaymentResponse(stripePaymentAdapter.createPaymentIntent(toParams(request)).id)
        }
}
```
